  "difficulty_reason": "After the named Floer-theoretic and Lusternik-Schnirelman prerequisites are supplied, the original argument transports the filtered open-closed spectral comparison to an abstract completed exact Lagrangian and uses a Hamiltonian constant on its compact spectral support to force equality of all base-class spectral levels. It constructs a proper radial extension with invariant minmax values and localizes each nonzero cohomology class into every support neighborhood, passing to the neighborhood cohomology limit. This Floer/spectral topology of nonsmooth completed Lagrangians is substantially beyond qualification-level manifold duality or ordinary Morse inequalities.",
